  "review_packet_sha256": "881f8ef77778f0f39240028dc0b8904af98404415d666b77f930c2792e136e92",
  "method": "Two PSFs with common shifts, free elliptical PSF and sloping sky in both hypotheses. Central: one free-centroid elliptical extended component. Paired hosts: independent nonnegative flux, scale, ellipticity and orientation at each point image. Repeat with Gaussian and exponential profiles. Positive paired-host-minus-central score favours central light. Scores use the previously measured blank-sky variance inflation and effective-pixel log penalty, not calibrated posterior odds. Gaussian size is major-axis sigma; exponential size is major-axis scale length. Residual montages use an identical scale.",
  "limits": "Seeing, PSF mismatch, bright knots, asymmetric coalescing hosts and projected galaxies remain ambiguous; a preferred central component provides no foreground redshift and no evidence of a repeated quasar spectrum."
}
